.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt FIND 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm find
.Nd walk a file hierarchy (sbase)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl H | Fl L
.Ar path ...
.Op Ar expression ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is sbase 0.1's
.Nm find ,
built for ABSD with the C kit and one declared patch
.Pq Pa userland/patches/find-absd.patch ;
see
.Xr sbase 7 .
It walks each
.Ar path
and evaluates the expression
.Pq Ic -name , Ic -type , Ic -size , Ic -prune , Ic -depth , Ic -print , No and the operators Ic \&! , Ic -a , Ic -o
for every object it finds, printing the paths for which it is true.
.Pp
It walks with
.Fn lstat ,
.Fn stat ,
.Fn opendir
and
.Fn readdir .
Each directory's listing is a snapshot that holds no handle, so depth
costs memory, not one of the 64 open files.
Output order is the file server's listing order, not sorted.
.Pp
What ABSD cannot do is refused while the expression is parsed, before any
path is visited, so nothing is printed first.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic -exec , Ic -ok
status 1,
.Ql find: -exec: cannot run commands on this system: Function not implemented ,
before any output
.Pq Ic -ok No likewise ;
commands cannot spawn.
.It Ic -atime , Ic -ctime , Ic -mtime , Ic -newer
status 1,
.Ql find: -atime/-ctime/-mtime/-newer: file times are not available on this system ,
before any output.
.It Ic -type l , Ic -type p/s/b/c
never true: only files and directories exist (A13).
.It Ic -perm
predicted: compares the reported modes, 0644 or 0444 (directories too, no
search bits):
.Ql -perm -200
selects writable objects.
.It Ic -nouser , Ic -nogroup , Ic -user Ar NAME , Ic -group Ar NAME
predicted: no user database on ABSD (CPA-050):
.Ic -nouser Ns / Ns Ic -nogroup
are true for every object, a name is
.Ql unknown user ,
status 1;
.Ql -user 1000
matches everything (SPEC A8).
.It Ic -xdev
compares
.Va st_dev ,
the filesystem id; mount boundaries in a session are unverified.
.It Fl H , Fl L
accepted; no symbolic links exist, so they change nothing.
.It an unreadable path
.Ql find: failed to stat PATH: <strerror>
and status 0, as upstream.
.El
.Pp
Behaviour on ABSD is predicted until the guest qualification
.Pq Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success (also after an unreadable path, as upstream); 1 on an error,
or one of the refusals above.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ find /home/operator -name '*.c'
absd$ find /var/log -type f -size +10
absd$ find . -name 'ed.*' -type f
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr grep 1 ,
.Xr intro 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7 ,
.Xr sbase 7
